  [1munrelated file is touched[0m. The alternative — rooting the whole project as ESM and renaming those two files to [38;5;153m.cjs[39m —
  is arguably tidier long-term but drags unrelated files into this change, so I'm not proposing it.

  [1mTest plan[0m — [38;5;153mnode --test[39m, built into Node, no dependency:

  - [38;5;153mrules.test.js[39m — each factory: pass, fail, custom vs. default message, whitespace-only input against [38;5;153mrequired[39m,
    [38;5;153mmatches[39m reading [38;5;153mallValues[39m.
  - [38;5;153mvalidate.test.js[39m — clean object; multiple failing fields; first-failure-wins per field; unknown field in values
    ignored; schema field missing from values treated as empty; empty schema.
  - [38;5;153mbind-form.test.js[39m — only if we have a DOM (see below).

  The pure modules get real coverage with zero setup. [38;5;153mbind-form[39m is the gap: testing it needs a DOM, and Node has none.

  [1mTooling.[0m The repo has no linter, formatter, test script, or CI — and this is the cheapest moment it will ever be to
  add them. Below is what I'd set up; tell me which you want.

  My recommendation is the first two: [38;5;153mnode --test[39m wired to [38;5;153mnpm test[39m, plus jsdom as a [1mdev[0mdependency so [38;5;153mbindForm[39m is
  actually tested. jsdom costs nothing at runtime — the shipped page stays zero-dependency — and without it the DOM
  layer, which is the half most likely to break, has no automated coverage at all. A formatter I'd take or leave at this
  size; end-to-end infrastructure I think is overkill for one form and I'd skip it.
